cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Alice in academic work, in a methodology you publish, or as a framework you cite, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "Alice — A framework for deriving your own agent-augmented operating system"
abstract: >-
  Alice is a tool-agnostic methodology for designing and running a personal
  or small-team agent-augmented operating system. It captures the decision
  process behind building a setup (skills, agent profiles, crons, rules)
  rather than shipping a snapshot of one operator's choices. The output of
  applying Alice is the reader's own setup, derived from their own context.
authors:
  - name: "042Trix"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-09-05"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/042Trix/Alice
